    "claim": "A capability that can only fail at a service the sandbox lacks needs a WIRE-SHAPE check, not an end-to-end one.",
    "detail": "Recall layer 4 shipped injecting its pack as a second system message and every sandbox check passed: with no LLM configured the provider call fails before the wire shape matters, so the honest-error assertion was satisfied by the wrong error. The fix is to intercept the call and assert the payload — tools/smoke/agent-app.mjs routes /app/exec, captures chat_llm's args, and asserts exactly one system message at index 0 with the pack inside it. tools/smoke/regress-syspack.mjs proves that check fails on the buggy form by reinstalling it on a disposable and restoring.",
    "tags": "testing,workflow,agent,llm",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1785964641069
  },
  {
    "claim": "When a dependency looks missing, establish whether it is VENDORED or GENERATED before concluding anything.",
    "detail": "newbound emits one rust crate per distinct \"root\" across data/*/meta.json — agent, kb, scratch, newbound_core, and cmd are all GENERATED by `newbound rebuild`, not vendored. cmd/ is absent from the mirror only because the store library that roots there (data/loradude_admin) is redacted; git history shows its generated shape (Cargo.toml + api.rs + cmdinit.rs + lib.rs) with no ML dependency at all. A generated artifact is yours to produce: tools/gen-cmd-crate.py writes the empty scaffold and canon builds with the owner's Cargo.toml unmodified. Two traps this closes: /cmd is gitignored BECAUSE it is generated, so the surface-before-overriding rule for deliberate gitignore lines does not apply to it; and the comment explaining why something was disabled can be older than the reason — this one still said \"needs CUDA + deps missing from this snapshot\" long after the owner removed those libraries. Commenting out an owner's dependency to route around a file you can generate is learned helplessness, and he named it as such.",
    "tags": "build,rust,workflow,platform-api",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1785971355573
  },
